{{also|kartoffel}}
==German==
{{wikipedia|lang=de}}

===Etymology===
{{borrowing|it|tartuficolo|t=[[truffle]]|lang=de}}, from {{der|de|ML.|*territūberum}}.<ref>{{R:EWddS|hw=Kartoffel|ed=22}}</ref>

The use as an ethnic nickname is due to the prominence of potatoes in German cuisine, particularly vis-à-vis the cuisines of the major allochthone communities in the country. (Compare the corresponding {{m|de|Spagetti}} used to refer to Italians.)

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/kaʁˈtɔfəl/|[kaʁˈtɔfl̩]|[kaɐ̯ˈtɔfl̩]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-at-Kartoffel.ogg|audio (Austria)|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Kartoffel.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Kartoffeln}}

# [[potato]]
# {{lb|de|derogatory}} a [[German]]; particularly an [[ethnic]] German from the perspective of [[allochthone]] populations in Germany

